---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Privacy Policy - TradeGuard</title>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 min-h-screen font-sans selection:bg-sky-500 selection:text-white">
    
    <!-- Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="flex justify-between items-center p-6 border-b border-slate-800 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/" class="text-xl font-bold text-sky-400 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>🛡️</span> TradeGuard <span class="text-xs bg-sky-950 text-sky-400 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-sky-800">PRO</span>
      </a>
      <div class="flex space-x-6 text-sm">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-sky-400 transition">Home</a>
        <a href="/terms" class="hover:text-sky-400 transition">Terms of Service</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 space-y-10">
      <div class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm">Last Updated: October 15, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <section class="bg-slate-800/60 p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-700 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-sky-400">1. Core Commitment: Zero Remote Data Collection</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
          TradeGuard Assistant ("the Extension") is designed with a privacy-first, zero-knowledge architecture. 
          <strong>We do not collect, store, transmit, process, or sell any personal data, browsing history, credentials, or trading metrics to any remote servers or third parties.</strong>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">2. Local IPC Communication Only</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
          The Extension functions solely as a local sensor for the TradeGuard desktop application:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base space-y-2">
          <li>
            All real-time risk evaluations and discipline lockout calculations occur entirely on your local machine.
          </li>
          <li>
            Data exchange occurs exclusively via an isolated local WebSocket loopback connection (<code class="bg-slate-800 text-sky-300 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono">127.0.0.1:18090</code>) between the Extension and the local TradeGuard Desktop Application.
          </li>
          <li>
            No web requests, external telemetry, passwords, or session tokens are ever transmitted outside your personal device environment.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">3. Explanation of Extension Permissions</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
          To enforce strict trading discipline, the Extension requests only the minimal necessary Manifest V3 permissions:
        </p>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="bg-slate-800 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 text-xs md:text-sm space-y-1">
            <div class="font-bold text-sky-400">chrome.storage</div>
            <p class="text-slate-400">Used strictly to persist local state, UI configuration preferences, and active lockout timers within your local browser storage.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-800 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 text-xs md:text-sm space-y-1">
            <div class="font-bold text-sky-400">chrome.alarms</div>
            <p class="text-slate-400">Used to maintain background connection keep-alive heartbeat timers with the local desktop agent.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-800 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-700 text-xs md:text-sm space-y-1 md:col-span-2">
            <div class="font-bold text-sky-400">Host Permissions & WebSockets</div>
            <p class="text-slate-400">Used solely to intercept local trading execution packets on supported broker platforms in real-time memory to trigger HUD overlays and discipline rules.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">4. Data Sharing and Sale</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
          Because TradeGuard does not collect any user data, we do not share, sell, transfer, or use user data for advertising, credit evaluation, or analytics under any circumstances.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">5. Contact Us</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
          If you have any questions regarding this Privacy Policy or TradeGuard's local security model, please contact us at:
        </p>
        <p class="text-sky-400 font-semibold text-sm md:text-base">
          ✉️ <a href="mailto:support@gettradeguard.app" class="hover:underline">support@gettradeguard.app</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="py-8 text-center text-xs text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-800 space-y-3">
      <p>© 2026 TradeGuard Project. Dedicated risk enforcement for smart traders.</p>
      <p class="space-x-4">
        <a href="/privacy" class="text-sky-400 transition underline">Privacy Policy</a>
        <span>•</span>
        <a href="/terms" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-400 transition underline">Terms of Service</a>
      </p>
    </footer>

  </body>
</html>